&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify'>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>BIBLE&lt;/span>&lt;/p>
&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify'>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>            Scripture
is the complete word of God written and sufficiently accurate in origin and
preservation to accomplish what God sent it to accomplish (Isaiah &lt;b>55&lt;/b>:11).
He sent it through chosen representatives endowed with the messages he revealed
to them and with the ability to correctly express it to the ones he wanted to
hear it. Consequently, non-canonical writings have the status, at best, of
devotional writings (Apocrypha and tradition).&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>WHAT CHRISTIANS IDEALLY BELIEVE AND PRACTICE: A SUMMARY DESCRIPTION</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/doctrinal-summaries/what-christians-ideally-believe-and-practice-a-summary-description/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/doctrinal-summaries/what-christians-ideally-believe-and-practice-a-summary-description/</guid><description>&lt;style>
